      {
        "id": 221604,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-08-23T18:33:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If you have all the expansions, then the only other things are the variants.</p><p>There are 4 commercial variant packs: the foil oversized villain pack,&nbsp;<span>the oversized villain pack (which is redundant if you own the foils, but if you're really a completionist, they're a separate thing), the foil hero pack, and the complete hero variant pack (again, redundant if you own the foils).</span></p><p><span>Then there's the original promo variants.&nbsp; Here's where things get hard.&nbsp; They were mostly limited releases, and most are out of print.&nbsp; The original Young Legacy in particular is rare and worth quite a bit.&nbsp; But there's one of these for every variant, including villain variants.&nbsp; Argent Adept does have one weird one: the \"original\" is Kvothe Six-String and the \"collector's edition\" is the Dark Conductor.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:54:19.190Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 3,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 15.0,
